See: [http://home.vicnet.net.au/~ozlit/edit9831.html

Australian] poetic movement, ca 1938/1948, distinguished by its attempt to "become indigenous" by using a smattering of words from Aboriginal languages, and the concept of the ((Dreamtime)). Basically, they felt that up until that time, Australian poets had been viewing their land through a filter of European diction, metaphors, and attitudes; and they wanted to show it as it really was, experienced by settlers with the same authenticity as the people who were already there when they arrived.

See also [http://www.africana.com/Articles/tt_242.htm|Negritude].
